# Only these networks may connect. Written by Terraform.
#
# Everyone else is sent to a path that no route of the site serves. A plain
# "respond @outside 403" here would never run: Caddy orders it after the
# "handle" blocks of the Caddyfile, which answer every request first. The
# rewrite is ordered before them (and before basic_auth). The respond line
# takes over, with a proper 403, if the Caddyfile ever sets
# "order respond before basic_auth".
@tersect_outside not remote_ip ${join(" ", allowed_cidrs)}
rewrite @tersect_outside /.forbidden
respond @tersect_outside "Forbidden" 403
